/-!
# Binary products for the HS normalizer's Sylow calculation

Ten explicit graph automorphisms generate a subgroup of the exact normalizer.
The 1024 ascending binary products are the finite family to be checked for
coverage, order and involution fusion. This module proves membership, without
assuming any of those additional assertions. The retained GAP script supplies
only candidate tables; inverse tables convert its right action to Lean's left
action, as in the definition of the HS carrier.

Source context: Aschbacher–Smith 16.1.5(10), p.1172; GLS3 Table 5.3m.
-/

